* .ac dec 100 10 10Meg
* Voltage sensing cct with 2nd order low pass filter, fcutoff at 10KHz.\nThis cct used to see bode plot of voltage sensing.
* .op
* Current sensing cct with 2nd order low pass filter, fcutoff at 10KHz.\nThis cct used to see bode plot of current sensing.
* Voltage zero crosssing detector\nDetects Vvf signal crosses the 2.1V Vref and creates a square wave.
* Ideal sources used for bode plot analysis of filters
* Voltage conditioning cct with 2nd order low pass filter\n \n- Difference amplifier with virtual ground used to amplify and shift voltage signal. \n- Total fcutoff at 10KHz by having all poles at 10KHz. \n- Second order filter created by cascading 2 first order low pass filters together.
* Current conditioning cct with 2nd order low pass filter\n \n- Difference amplifier with virtual ground used to amplify and shift current shunt resistor voltage signal. \n- Total fcutoff at 10KHz by having all poles at 10KHz. \n- Second order filter created by cascading 2 first order low pass filters together.
* Current sens: 0.5Ohm\nPmax = 180mW
* Load \n(2.5VA-7.5VA)
* 5V DC to 2.1V using voltage divider + Voltage follower\nVref: 2.1V
* Half wave rectifier with a 5V regulator to get 5V
* ***************************\nELECTENG 209 - Team 15\nProgress review\n***************************
* Simulation commands
* - Rload is the variable resistor in the load which changes\n  from 5-105 ohms.\n- Vsupply is between 12.6-15.4Vrms.
* Current zero crosssing detector\nDetects Vif signal crosses the 2.1V Vref and creates a square wave.
